Z||000000||jch82||10-28-2001||01:03 AM||||Here's the dilemma. I changed the belt in my 84 SE and tightened it back up. It started squealing and eventually would stop when I started moving. I put some belt dressing on it. That helped for oh say a day....Now it squeals but it doesnt seem to go with the engines rpm's like it did before. its more of a constant squeal and it goes away sometimes. could this be my alternator saying that it wants to die?? any information would be very very helpful! thanks!!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
